From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 23:07:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm: show the GUI frame-sequentially with the video's eye

For frame-sequential 3D the GUI has to change eye with the video on every
vsync. The legacy OSD driver had a frame-alternative mode; the DRM VPU
pipeline the GUI goes through on S6 has none, and it writes the OSD
registers only on an atomic commit, into a vsync RDMA table the hardware
then replays every vsync (the DRM RDMA irq count rises by the refresh rate
with no new config).

With osd_fa_3d (aml_drm parameter) set to 1 (side by side) or 2 (top and
bottom), the client draws both eyes into one framebuffer:
- the primary plane on VPP0 scans out one half, so the scaler is set up
  half to full by the usual path;
- every commit writes the OSD fetch window for the eye the video layer
  chose for the next frame, with the mode and the eye offset it was built
  for, and always writes it so the window is in every table;
- the vsync hooks (the VPU vsync irq, and the video layer's right
  after it publishes the eye) move the window inside the armed table when the eye moves
  on, in one pass over the table (rdma_table_patch_regs(), under
  rdma_lock).
A vsync the video handler dropped leaves the generation, so the GUI keeps
the video's eye; with the video in 2D the GUI shows the first eye; a GFCD
(AFBC/AFRC) plane is left alone.

Measured on an S905X5: the window registers alternate between the two
halves on successive vsyncs, on the eye the video shows.

The mode is latched when the commit is checked, with the distance between
the two halves, and the commit and the vsync hook use only that: the
parameter changing between the check and a non-blocking commit's tail
cannot make the right-eye window read past a framebuffer of one eye's
height, or move it the wrong way. The window is moved only if both eyes'
windows lie inside the framebuffer.

Only the plane the window logic moves is halved: the primary plane of
VPP0, on a linear framebuffer (an AFBC or AFRC one, through the MIF or
GFCD, is fetched outside the MIF window), outside slice mode (the SoC's,
above 60 Hz, or forced by osd_slice_mode). On a canvas SoC the canvas
covers the whole framebuffer, so the second eye is inside it. A disabled
OSD stops being moved.

A commit stages its blocks (window, distance, drops) apart from those of
the armed table, and they become the ones the hook moves only once their
table is armed: a vsync between the two moved the old table by the new
layout (on entering 3D, eye 1 read rows 1080-2159 of a 1080-row
framebuffer). The VPP0 table is armed under osd_fa_lock, and in the same
hold the staged blocks become current and the window is set again for the
current eye, since the eye was sampled when the table was built: a hook
on another CPU can never patch the newly armed table with the previous
blocks (leaving 3D, that kept eye 1's window, rows 1080-2159 of a 1080-row
framebuffer, until the next GUI commit). The video layer
also calls the window update right after publishing each eye
(amvideo_set_fa_notify()), so the GUI follows the vsync's own eye
whatever order the two handlers on the shared vsync line run in; the
update is done once per eye generation. osd_fa_lock is always taken
before rdma_lock.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/drm/meson_plane.c b/drivers/drm/meson_plane.c
index eafb397..caa9aed 100644
--- a/drivers/drm/meson_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/meson_plane.c
@@ -346,7 +346,11 @@ meson_plane_position_calc(struct meson_vpu_osd_layer_info *plane_info,
 	struct drm_crtc *crtc = state->crtc;
 	struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state;
 	struct drm_display_mode *mode;
+	struct meson_vpu_data *vpu_data;
+	int fa;
 
+	plane_info->fa_mode = 0;
+	plane_info->fa_shift = 0;
 	if (crtc) {
 		crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_crtc_state(atomic_state, crtc);
 		mode = &crtc_state->mode;
@@ -363,6 +367,29 @@ meson_plane_position_calc(struct meson_vpu_osd_layer_info *plane_info,
 	plane_info->src_y = state->src_y >> 16;
 	plane_info->src_w = (state->src_w >> 16) & 0xffff;
 	plane_info->src_h = (state->src_h >> 16) & 0xffff;
+	/*
+	 * frame-sequential 3D: the GUI holds both eyes, scan out one half. Only
+	 * where the commit can move the window: the primary plane of VPP0, a
+	 * linear framebuffer (AFBC/AFRC/GFCD fetch outside the MIF window), no
+	 * slice mode. The mode is latched here for the commit.
+	 */
+	fa = meson_osd_fa_mode();
+	vpu_data = pipeline->priv ? pipeline->priv->vpu_data : NULL;
+	if (fa && crtc->index == 0 && state->plane &&
+	    state->plane->type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY &&
+	    state->fb && !state->fb->modifier && !meson_osd_slice_mode() &&
+	    !(vpu_data && vpu_data->slice_mode == 1 &&
+	      drm_mode_vrefresh(mode) > 60)) {
+		if (fa == 1 && plane_info->src_w >= 2) {
+			plane_info->src_w >>= 1;
+			plane_info->fa_shift = plane_info->src_w;
+			plane_info->fa_mode = fa;
+		} else if (fa == 2 && plane_info->src_h >= 2) {
+			plane_info->src_h >>= 1;
+			plane_info->fa_shift = plane_info->src_h;
+			plane_info->fa_mode = fa;
+		}
+	}
 
 	DRM_DEBUG("original source: src_x=%d, src_y=%d, src_w=%d, src_h=%d\n",
 		plane_info->src_x, plane_info->src_y, plane_info->src_w, plane_info->src_h);
